    "description": "StartFragment\n\nGoal Tracker API v1\n\nThis collection documents and tests the Goal Tracker backend for authentication, user profile access, and goal CRUD operations.\n\nWhat this API includes:\n\n- Health check endpoint to verify API uptime.\n    \n- User registration and login.\n    \n- Current user profile endpoint.\n    \n- Protected user listing endpoint.\n    \n- Goal create, read, update, and delete endpoints.\n    \n\nAuthentication model:\n\n- Login and register return a JWT access token in the response body.\n    \n- Login and register also set an httpOnly accessToken cookie for browser-based auth.\n    \n- Protected endpoints accept either:\n    \n\n1. accessToken cookie\n    \n2. Authorization: Bearer header (recommended for mobile/API clients)\n    \n\nResponse format:\n\n- Success responses use a consistent envelope with success, statusCode, message, and data.\n    \n- Error responses include statusCode, message, errors, and success=false.\n    \n- Validation errors return 422 with field-level details in errors\\[\\].\n    \n\nHow to use this collection:\n\n1. Set the collection variable baseUrl (example: [http://localhost:5000/api/v1](https://null)).\n    \n2. Run Register or Login first.\n    \n3. For token-based flow, store data.accessToken and send it as Bearer token.\n    \n4. For cookie-based flow, let Postman manage cookies automatically.\n    \n5. Test protected routes like /user/me and /goals after authentication.\n    \n\nNotes:\n\n- Token lifetime is 24 hours.\n    \n- Goal title is required and has a max length of 100.\n    \n- Goal update/delete expects a valid MongoDB ObjectId in path params.\n    \n\nEndFragment",
