      "description": "This folder covers end-to-end authentication and protected user access for Goal Tracker API v1.\n\nFlow covered\n\n1. Register User  \n    Creates a new account with username, email, and password.  \n    On success, server returns data.accessToken and also sets accessToken as an httpOnly cookie.  \n    Validation errors return 422 with field-level errors.\n    \n2. Login User  \n    Authenticates using email and password.  \n    On success, server returns data.accessToken and refreshes accessToken cookie.\n    \n3. Get My Profile (Cookie Flow)  \n    Calls GET /user/me using Postman cookie jar after login/register.  \n    Use this to verify browser-style session auth.\n    \n4. Get My Profile (Bearer Flow)  \n    Calls GET /user/me using Authorization header with Bearer token from collection variable accessToken.  \n    Use this to verify mobile/client token auth.\n    \n5. Get All Users  \n    Protected route GET /user/all-users.  \n    Requires valid cookie or Bearer token.\n    \n6. Logout User  \n    Calls POST /user/logout on authenticated session.  \n    Clears accessToken cookie and returns success response.\n    \n\nExpected auth behavior\n\n1. Protected endpoints accept either cookie token or Bearer token.\n    \n2. Missing/invalid/expired token returns 401.\n    \n3. Token expiry is 24 hours.\n    \n\nCollection variable usage\n\n1. baseUrl should point to [http://localhost:5000/api/v1](https://null)\n    \n2. accessToken should be auto-set from register/login test scripts.\n    \n3. Prefer cookie flow for browser simulation and Bearer flow for mobile/API simulation.\n    \n\nRecommended run order\n\n1. Register User\n    \n2. Login User\n    \n3. Get My Profile (Cookie)\n    \n4. Get My Profile (Bearer)\n    \n5. Get All Users\n    \n6. Logout User\n    \n7. Optional: run Get My Profile again to confirm unauthorized after logout (401 expected)."
