      "description": "This folder contains all authenticated goal operations for Goal Tracker. Use it to create, read, update, and delete user goals in a complete lifecycle flow.\n\nWhat this folder covers\n\n1. Get Goals  \n    GET /goals  \n    Returns all goals created by the authenticated user.\n    \n2. Create Goal  \n    POST /goals  \n    Creates a new goal for the authenticated user.  \n    Required body field:\n    \n\n- title (required, max length 100)\n    \n\n1. Update Goal  \n    PUT /goals/:id  \n    Updates an existing goal title by goal id.  \n    Required:\n    \n\n- valid goal id in path\n    \n- title in body (required, max length 100)\n    \n\n1. Delete Goal  \n    DELETE /goals/:id  \n    Deletes a goal by goal id.  \n    Required:\n    \n\n- valid goal id in path\n    \n\nAuthentication requirements\n\n1. All routes in this folder are protected.\n    \n2. You can authenticate using either:\n    \n\n- accessToken cookie (browser-style flow)\n    \n- Authorization: Bearer header (mobile/client flow)\n    \n\nValidation and errors\n\n1. Validation errors return status 422 with field-level details.\n    \n2. Unauthorized or invalid token returns status 401.\n    \n3. Invalid goal id format returns validation error.\n    \n4. Standard error response includes:\n    \n\n- statusCode\n    \n- message\n    \n- errors\n    \n- success false\n    \n\nSuccess response format  \nAll successful goal CRUD responses follow the API success envelope with:\n\n- success true\n    \n- statusCode\n    \n- message\n    \n- data\n    \n\nRecommended execution order in Postman\n\n1. Create Goal\n    \n2. Get Goals\n    \n3. Update Goal\n    \n4. Get Goals\n    \n5. Delete Goal\n    \n6. Get Goals\n    \n\nFolder variables suggestion\n\n1. baseUrl = [http://localhost:5000/api/v1](https://null)\n    \n2. accessToken = set from login/register response\n    \n3. goalId = set from Create Goal response data._id"
